# Agentic Workflow

This project follows specification-driven development.

The canonical flow is:

Problem
→ PRD
→ Specification
→ Architecture
→ Implementation Plan
→ Implementation
→ Tests
→ Review
→ Verification

Agents have separate responsibilities.

## Product agent

May create or modify:

docs/PRD.md

Must not implement application code.

## Specification agent

May create or modify:

docs/SPEC.md

Must translate requirements into testable behavior.

Must not implement application code.

## Architect agent

May create or modify:

docs/ARCHITECTURE.md

Must make technical decisions and explain trade-offs.

Must not implement application code.

## Developer agent

May modify application code only after:

PRD.md
SPEC.md
ARCHITECTURE.md
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md

exist.

## Test agent

Focuses on behavioral correctness and edge cases.

It should attempt to find defects rather than merely confirm implementation.

## Reviewer agent

Must independently review the implementation.

It must not assume that the developer's solution is correct.

## Conflicts

If implementation reveals a contradiction in the specification:

STOP.

Report:

SPECIFICATION_CONFLICT

Explain the conflict before changing requirements.